      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. A single 8,500 mg dose is about 10 times the maximum daily dose, and the order would give 25,500 mg per day. I can't think of a clinical situation where that would be appropriate. It carries a serious risk of life-threatening lactic acidosis. Your confirmation doesn't change that.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **If it was a typo:** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals right now, or any dose up to the 2,550 mg/day maximum.\n- **If there's a clinical reason I don't know about:** please talk to the pharmacist or attending first. If they approve it, it would need to go through a pharmacy-verified override, not through me.\n- **If a patient may have already taken a large amount of metformin:** this is an overdose. Contact poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US) or toxicology, and check lactate and acid-base status.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
      }
     ],
